BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-fund-enter-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Fund: ENTER 2026 (exploratory cross-border
  collaboration)
DESCRIPTION:ENTER is the first programme in the Nordic Culture Fund's new p
 ortfolio\, designed to support ambitious ideas that need collaboration to 
 be explored and tested in practice. It offers space to experiment\, learn 
 as you go and test new directions through encounters across disciplines an
 d perspectives\, rather than funding finished productions. WHO CAN APPLY: 
 individuals\, groups\, organisations\, institutions\, associations and com
 panies\, from arts and culture or other sectors\, as long as arts and cult
 ure are central to the initiative. Initiatives need clear Nordic anchoring
  (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\; applicants and pa
 rtners may be based anywhere\, and multiple applications for different ini
 tiatives are permitted. FUNDING: up to DKK 50\,000\, plus up to DKK 25\,00
 0 in accessibility support\, with no co-funding requirement. WHAT IT DOES 
 NOT SUPPORT: education or study visits\, conference or festival participat
 ion\, tours or travelling exhibitions\, productions or publications\, orga
 nisational running costs\, or construction and equipment purchases. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted electronically through the Fund's portal in Danish\, Norw
 egian\, Swedish\, Finnish or English\; no attachments are allowed\, so eve
 rything must fit in the form. Decisions come within five weeks of the dead
 line. The autumn 2026 window runs 14 September to 16 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Nordic Culture Fund\nLocation: Nordic region and beyond. Initiat
 ives must have clear Nordic anchoring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-bor
 der collaboration\, but applicants and partners may be based anywhere.\nAw
 ard: Up to DKK 50\,000 (roughly EUR 6\,700)\, plus up to DKK 25\,000 in ad
 ditional accessibility support for logistics and access needs\, for a maxi
 mum total of DKK 75\,000. No co-funding required. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects may run up to one year from the stated start date\, genera
 lly non-extendable.\n\nMore: https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-prog
 rammes/give-ambitious-ideas-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-programmes/give-ambitious-idea
 s-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Nordic region and beyond. Initiatives must have clear Nordic ancho
 ring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\, but applicant
 s and partners may be based anywhere.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:social-shifters-global-innovation-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Social Shifters Global Innovation Challenge 2026
DESCRIPTION:Social Shifters\, a Scottish-registered charity backed by corpo
 rate partners\, runs its Global Innovation Challenge as a funnel into a lo
 nger founder-development pipeline rather than a one-off prize. ELIGIBILITY
 : founders aged 18 to 30 at submission\, leading a fully youth-led venture
  that is already live and producing measurable social or environmental imp
 act\, aligned to at least one Sustainable Development Goal\; concept-stage
  ideas and student projects do not qualify. Multiple winners receive up to
  USD 15\,000 each\, plus pitch coaching\, a finalist showcase\, and ongoin
 g access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netw
 ork. Free coaching is available from the moment you register\, so the payo
 ff to registering early is high. Submissions close 31 August 2026 (5pm UTC
 )\, with finalists announced in October and winners in December 2026. Appl
 y at https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Social Shifters\nLocation: Global\; open to youth-led ventures fro
 m anywhere in the world.\nAward: Multiple awards of up to USD 15\,000 each
  (reported grants from USD 3\,000 to USD 15\,000)\, plus pitch coaching\, 
 a finalist showcase\, free founder support from registration\, and ongoing
  access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netwo
 rk that corporate partners recruit from. Free to enter.\nDuration: Submiss
 ions close 31 August 2026\; finalists announced October\, winners December
  2026\n\nMore: https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global\; open to youth-led ventures from anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernest-solvay-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: King Baudouin Foundation: Ernest Solvay Fund 2026 (Call f
 or Projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Ernest Solvay Fund provides financial support for local-imp
 act initiatives in three areas: scientific education (science\, technology
 \, engineering and mathematics)\, planet progress (environmental initiativ
 es) and better life (community well-being). ELIGIBILITY: organisations sub
 mitting a project must implement it within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site. FUNDING: up to EUR 10\,000 per initi
 ative\; the Fund covers expenses incurred only after the results are annou
 nced (mid-December 2026) and will not reimburse expenses incurred beforeha
 nd. APPLY: create or log in to an account at https://candidate.kbs-frb.be 
 and complete the online application form (it can be saved and completed in
  several stages). Applications are open 15 April 2026 to 30 September 2026
 \; results announced mid-December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Ernest Solv
 ay\, managed with the support of the King Baudouin Foundation\nLocation: O
 rganisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site\nAward: Up to EUR 10\,000 per initiat
 ive. Funding covers only expenses incurred after the results are announced
  (mid-December 2026)\; already-incurred expenses are not reimbursed. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Project implemented after mid-December 2026 anno
 uncement\n\nMore: https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Organisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a S
 olvay industrial\, R&I or administrative site
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count). The inviting foreig
 n party must cover a proportionate share of the costs. Covers hourly fees\
 , travel and accommodation directly related to the activity. IMPORTANT TIM
 ING RULE: applications are accepted from 5 months to a minimum of 7 weeks 
 before the activity begins\, and processing takes about 6 weeks. This lead
  time can rule out activities that fall shortly after a round opens. Round
  2 (4 May to 22 June 2026) has closed. Round 3 runs 8 September 2026 15:00
  CEST to 27 October 2026 16:00 CEST\, with a budget of EUR 33\,000\; given
  the 7-week rule it effectively serves activities starting from late Octob
 er 2026 onwards. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: you must already have had an appl
 ication to the Fund positively assessed within the past five years\, and a
  previous voucher does not satisfy this\, so this is not a viable first ap
 proach to the Fund. The window runs 8 September 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 27 Oc
 tober 2026\, but closes early once 20 complete applications are received. 
 Maximum one voucher per applicant per calendar year.\n\nOrganisation: Stim
 uleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation:
  Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within Eur
 ope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per trip
 \n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-voucher
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:onx-seeds-soft-circuits-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Onassis ONX: ONX Seeds 2026\, Soft Circuits for Hard Time
 s (Athens\, hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:ONX Seeds 2026 is a four-month incubation and seed funding prog
 ram run by Onassis ONX\, the Onassis Foundation's platform for art and adv
 anced technologies\, hosted in Athens in a hybrid format under the theme S
 oft Circuits for Hard Times. It invites emerging artists\, creative techno
 logists\, designers\, game makers\, performers\, sound and visual artists 
 and makers (individuals\, groups and collectives\, Greek and international
 ) to develop early-stage prototypes that make the digital tangible: intera
 ctive objects\, wearable or embedded systems\, screen-based worlds\, parti
 cipatory environments\, games\, rituals\, sonic works\, moving images and 
 hybrid analogue-digital forms. Proposals should be realistic in scope and 
 result in an exhibitable prototype. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed fun
 ding per project\, weekly technical mentoring plus curatorial and business
  mentoring and online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams (remote participation for everyone else)\,
  presentation at ONX Exhibition Athens (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\,
  accommodation and artwork transport covered for non-Athens participants\,
  and connections to the ONX network in Athens\, New York and beyond. HOW T
 O APPLY: via the Onassis open calls portal\, with project summary\, concep
 t\, visitor experience\, technical requirements\, production plan and bio\
 , plus a mood board or project deck\, portfolio and development budget as 
 single PDFs\; technical documentation and links to demos or repositories o
 ptional. DEADLINE: 26 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Onassis ONX (Onassis 
 Foundation)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators f
 rom Greece and internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams
 .\nAward: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed funding per project\, set by scope\; u
 p to four projects selected. Plus weekly technical\, curatorial and busine
 ss mentoring\, online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams\, and presentation at ONX Exhibition Athen
 s (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\, accommodation and artwork transport 
 covered for non-Athens participants. No application fee.\nDuration: Four-m
 onth incubation\, culminating in ONX Exhibition Athens\, 17 to 21 March 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-har
 d-times-2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times-2?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Greece and 
 internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unearthodox-exploration-co-lab-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261117
SUMMARY:Deadline: Unearthodox Exploration Co-Lab 2027: Edges of Possibility
DESCRIPTION:Online incubator from Swiss foundation Unearthodox (formerly th
 e Luc Hoffmann Institute) for innovators with early-stage ideas at the int
 ersection of environmental and societal challenges\, aimed at work that ta
 ckles root causes in the relationship between people\, society and nature 
 rather than symptoms: climate\, biodiversity\, habitat loss\, regeneration
  and environmental justice among them. WHAT YOU GET: a CHF 10\,000 grant p
 lus 10 months of cohort-based incubation (March to December 2027) with coa
 ching\, expert and peer support\, and access to a global community of syst
 ems innovators. ELIGIBILITY: over 18\, idea already in motion through rese
 arch\, testing\, piloting or community engagement\; applications in Englis
 h\; participation fully online with sessions planned for UTC-6 to UTC+6. S
 ELECTION CRITERIA: systems orientation (25 percent)\, nature-society visio
 n (25 percent)\, boundary-pushing (25 percent)\, transformational intent (
 15 percent)\, edge-walking (10 percent). DEADLINE: 16 November 2026\, 23:5
 9 GMT+1 (window opened 15 September 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Unearthodox\nL
 ocation: Online\; group sessions designed around time zones UTC-6 to UTC+6
 . Open worldwide to applicants over 18\; applications in English.\nAward: 
 CHF 10\,000 grant per selected initiative\, plus a 10-month incubation pro
 gramme with tailored coaching\, expert support\, peer learning\, systems m
 apping and futures-thinking support. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 mon
 ths\, 1 March to 31 December 2027\n\nMore: https://unearthodox.org/2026/09
 /open-call-edges-of-possibility-exploration-co-lab-2027/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unearthodox.org/2026/09/open-call-edges-of-possibility-explorat
 ion-co-lab-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\; group sessions designed around time zones UTC-6 to UTC+6.
  Open worldwide to applicants over 18\; applications in English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lendhauer-urban-ecologies-klagenfurt-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: Lendhauer: Urban Ecologies - Coexistence and Control (Len
 dhafen\, Klagenfurt 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Klagenfurt association Lendhauer invites proposals for artw
 orks at the Lendhafen\, the city's harbour\, under the 2027 theme Urban Ec
 ologies: Coexistence and Control. The call asks who or what counts as usef
 ul or disruptive in public space\, who is included or excluded\, and wheth
 er peaceful coexistence is achievable\, treating urban space as networks o
 f diverse relationships between human and non-human actors. Both fully dev
 eloped artistic works and experimental\, process-based or collaborative ap
 proaches are welcome. WHAT YOU GET: production costs up to EUR 4\,000 gros
 s (exact amount depends on project scope)\, an artist fee up to EUR 2\,500
  gross\, travel expenses up to EUR 1\,000\, and on-site coordination of te
 chnical and organisational requirements including permits. ELIGIBILITY: ar
 tists\, designers\, architects\, performers\, theorists and practitioners 
 working in interdisciplinary contexts\; individuals and collectives\, base
 d in Austria or abroad\; disciplines listed are architecture\, performing 
 arts\, and visual arts and design. Projects are realised June to end of Se
 ptember 2027. DEADLINE: 2 November 2026. Full details and application via 
 lendhafen.at.\n\nOrganisation: Lendhauer (Klagenfurt\, Austria)\nLocation:
  Lendhafen harbour\, Klagenfurt\, Austria. Open to individuals and collect
 ives based in Austria or abroad.\nAward: Artist fee up to EUR 2\,500 gross
 \, production costs up to EUR 4\,000 gross (depending on project scope)\, 
 and travel expenses up to EUR 1\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Proje
 cts realised at the Lendhafen between June and the end of September 2027.\
 n\nMore: https://www.lendhafen.at/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.lendhafen.at/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Lendhafen harbour\, Klagenfurt\, Austria. Open to individuals and 
 collectives based in Austria or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231809Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027: Energy G
 hosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:The Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Program is an annual fellow
 ship offering four fully funded fellowships to artists from around the wor
 ld\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with V
 ISIT\, the artist-in-residence programme of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK L
 uckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art (Warsaw). The
  2027 edition particularly encourages projects at the intersection of art\
 , energy and ecology exploring the theme ENERGY GHOSTS: the unseen dimensi
 ons of energy approached through mythology\, cosmology or speculative fict
 ion\, the invisible infrastructures\, histories and residues that haunt co
 ntemporary life\, and energy as an ecological\, political or spiritual for
 ce. Proposals are welcome from visual art\, performance\, film\, installat
 ion\, sound\, writing and new media. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 20\,000 per fellow 
 for artist fees and production costs of a new project (research and develo
 pment\, travel\, material and presentation costs)\; three fellows receive 
 studio space and accommodation at E-WERK Luckenwalde (a former power stati
 on about 40 minutes south of Berlin)\, one is accommodated by the Akademie
  der Künste in Berlin. The three-month residency runs roughly September t
 o November 2027 with on-site presence of at least 75% required\, a retreat
  at Ujazdowski Castle in Warsaw in September 2027\, events across the thre
 e venues\, and a closing symposium in October 2027 at the Akademie der Kü
 nste where fellows show work in progress alongside the 2026 cohort. JURY: 
 Nolan Oswald Dennis\; Chus Martinez (Institute Art Gender Nature\, TBA21)\
 ; Sarah Johanna Theurer (Fondation Beyeler)\; Anh-Linh Ngo (Akademie der K
 ünste)\; and Tiara Roxanne. APPLICATION: via the VISIT portal at visit-en
 ergy.com/bewerben. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation:
  JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-
 WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocati
 on: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie de
 r Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in
  Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fel
 lowships of EUR 20\,000 each\, intended for artist fees and production cos
 ts of a new project (research and development\, travel\, materials and pre
 sentation costs)\, plus studio space and accommodation for the three-month
  residency.\nDuration: Three months\, roughly September to November 2027 (
 the AdK notice gives mid-August to mid-November)\; fellows must live and w
 ork on site at least 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10
 /open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
